      "file_path": "db/migrations/0002_order_status.sql",
      "line_number": 3,
      "line_end": 3,
      "title": "Required column added to a populated table without a default",
      "description": "The migration adds status as NOT NULL with no default to the existing orders table. Postgres rejects this ALTER whenever orders already holds rows. The migration fails on any database with existing orders, so the deploy breaks. The new code in src/orders.js then queries a status column that does not exist. Add the column with a default, or add it nullable, backfill existing orders, then set NOT NULL. Choose the backfill value on purpose, because existing orders count as open if they get placed.",
      "suggested_change": "ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN status text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'placed';",
      "source": "squawk:adding-required-field",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The migration adds status as NOT NULL with no default to the existing orders table. Postgres rejects this ALTER whenever orders already holds rows.",
      "consequence": "The migration fails on any database with existing orders, so the deploy breaks. The new code in src/orders.js then queries a status column that does not exist.",
      "fix": "Add the column with a default, or add it nullable, backfill existing orders, then set NOT NULL. Choose the backfill value on purpose, because existing orders count as open if they get placed."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
