      "title": "Index build blocks writes to orders",
      "description": "The migration builds orders_customer_status_idx without CONCURRENTLY. Postgres blocks every write to orders until the build finishes. On a large orders table, createOrder calls stall or time out while the index builds. Build the index with CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY, outside a transaction.",
      "suggested_change": "CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY orders_customer_status_idx ON orders (customer_id, status);",
      "source": "squawk:require-concurrent-index-creation",
